Package: labelnoise
Title: Find Label Errors in Classification Data with Confident Learning
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ridson", "Al Farizal P", , "ridsonalfarizal15@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0617-0214"))
Description: Finds examples whose given class label is likely wrong, using
    out-of-sample predicted probabilities from any classifier. Implements
    confident learning (Northcutt, Jiang and Chuang, 2021)
    <doi:10.1613/jair.1.12125>: per-class confidence thresholds, the
    confident joint, calibrated estimates of the joint distribution of given
    and true labels, noise transition matrices, and five rank-and-prune
    rules for flagging label issues. Also provides model-agnostic label
    quality scores (Kuan and Mueller, 2022) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.18168246>
    and a per-class label health summary. Inputs can be a label vector with
    a probability matrix, a data frame of predictions, resampling results
    from 'tune', predictions from 'mlr3', or a fitted 'caret' model.
